# UX workflow: ADR-0015/0016 closeout authoring and runtime feedback smoke.
# Purpose: validates one dense end-user path across micro-sequence authoring,
# child quick controls, same-step cycle-state authoring, parent back navigation,
# root badges, resolved-value feedback, runtime playhead progress, and a visible
# active parent playhead marker.
# Expect: playhead_progress

0 scenario sequencer
50 capture screen sequencer_ready

# Enable root step 1, then open the parent step editor.
150 tap MACRO_1 60
320 capture screen root_step_enabled
420 button MACRO_1 down
1480 tick
1540 capture screen root_step_edit_open
1600 button MACRO_1 up

# Enter Micro-sequence from the parent editor.
1700 encoder NAV 1
1780 encoder NAV 1
1860 encoder NAV 1
1940 encoder NAV 1
2020 encoder NAV 1
2100 encoder NAV 1
2260 capture screen parent_micro_row_focused
2360 tap NAV 60
2660 capture screen micro_context_open

# Edit micro step 1 pitch, then apply.
2760 button MACRO_1 down
3820 tick
3880 capture screen micro_step_edit_open
3940 button MACRO_1 up
4040 encoder NAV 1
4140 encoder OPT 0.72
4360 capture screen micro_step_note_offset_visible
4460 tap NAV 60
4700 capture screen micro_step_note_offset_applied

# Child quick controls expose Length then Offset. This must feel like root
# sequencer wrapping but without a Division control.
4800 button LEFT_CENTER down
5060 capture screen micro_quick_length
5160 encoder NAV 1
5360 capture screen micro_quick_offset
5460 encoder OPT 0.80
5680 capture screen micro_offset_adjusted
5780 button LEFT_CENTER up
6060 capture screen micro_offset_applied

# Back to the root grid. Child contexts use LEFT_TOP as back-to-owner-grid, not
# back-to-parent-editor, so the parent step editor must be opened again before
# editing sibling child content.
6160 tap LEFT_TOP 60
6500 capture screen root_grid_after_micro_badge

# Re-open the same root step editor and create/open Cycle states on the sibling
# row. This captures the actual parent editor state instead of relying on
# stale focus after returning from MICRO.
6600 button MACRO_1 down
7660 tick
7720 capture screen root_step_edit_reopened_for_cycle
7780 button MACRO_1 up
7880 encoder NAV 1
7960 encoder NAV 1
8040 encoder NAV 1
8120 encoder NAV 1
8200 encoder NAV 1
8280 encoder NAV 1
8360 encoder NAV 1
8520 capture screen parent_cycle_row_focused
8620 tap NAV 60
9020 capture screen cycle_context_open

# Edit cycle state 1 note and active/gate feedback via the normal step editor.
9120 button MACRO_1 down
10180 tick
10240 capture screen cycle_state_step_edit_open
10300 button MACRO_1 up
10400 encoder NAV 1
10480 encoder OPT 0.86
10640 capture screen cycle_state_note_offset_visible
10720 encoder NAV 1
10800 encoder NAV 1
10880 encoder OPT 0.35
11040 capture screen cycle_state_gate_offset_visible
11140 tap NAV 60
11440 capture screen cycle_state_offsets_applied

# Back to root and verify compact badges plus currently resolved parent state.
11540 tap LEFT_TOP 60
11880 capture screen root_grid_badges_and_resolution

# Arm adjacent steps so playback captures include an active blue playhead, not
# only the inactive grey playhead passing over empty steps.
11980 tap MACRO_2 60
12080 tap MACRO_3 60
12180 tap MACRO_4 60
12480 capture screen root_grid_steps_armed_for_playback

# Playback should advance the runtime playhead trace and show a visible marker
# on the grid. Active steps should render the marker blue.
12580 tap BOTTOM_CENTER 60
12980 capture screen playback_feedback_start
13720 tick
13820 capture screen playback_feedback_later
13920 tap BOTTOM_CENTER 60
14240 capture screen playback_feedback_stopped
